kill","entries_at_kill","entries_lost","disruptions","effects_beyond_missing_heartbeat","verdict","refusals_by_reason","records"],"title":"DeathDrillReport v1 — the registrar's death drill at a moment: the first node ever started, every node's standing with its registry size and its liveness verdict on the first node, and the totals — kills, heartbeats sent, registrations and syncs before and after the kill, joins and lookups after the kill, entries held at the kill and entries lost, disruptions, and effects_beyond_missing_heartbeat; the verdict is passed only when the first node is gone on every survivor's tracker, the mesh kept registering, syncing, and admitting new nodes after the kill, and nothing was lost or disrupted — failed when anything was, incomplete until the drill has run that far; simulated is a constant — the kill is the in-process loss of one replica, no process was killed and no LAN was crossed (Y-067)","type":"object"}